  "id": "species-specific-behavior",
  "term": "species-specific behavior",
  "definition": "Species-specific behavior is the characteristic way members of a species act in relation to their environment, such as the kinds of resources or habitats they tend to choose from what is available. Studying these patterns can help show a species’ ecological relationships, resource needs, and how behavior may adapt under extreme conditions.",
